		(property "BOM Comments" "Reused from the v1 build - desoldered, not reordered. Deliberately NOT moved to LCSC: F1 is through-hole, so it is not on the SMD assembly BOM PCBWay sources, and the Littelfuse part is better than the LCSC alternatives on every axis that matters (Imax 100 A vs 40 A, 3.8 A trip vs 4.0 A, ~9-10 mm body vs 15.2 mm). If it ever does need reordering, buy it from DigiKey or Mouser alongside the Switchcraft RCA jacks, which cannot come from LCSC either. The closest LCSC parts are Jinrui JK30-200 (C369104, verified radial, but taller and only 40 A Imax) and JKSEMI JK16-200T (C5183874, whose datasheet is headed 'Surface Mount' despite LCSC listing it as through-hole - package unconfirmed, do not use without checking the mechanical drawing)."
